{"id":"917ca273e02be94c285354c400197cd99596846f","axis":"silent","repo":"envoyproxy/envoy","sha":"917ca273e02be94c285354c400197cd99596846f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"changelogs/current/bug_fixes/aws__destroy-route-level-signer-on-main-thread.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@","+Fixed a race where the route level configuration of the","+:ref:`AWS request signing <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.filters.http.aws_request_signing.v3.AwsRequestSigningPerRoute>`","+and :ref:`AWS Lambda <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.filters.http.aws_lambda.v3.PerRouteConfig>`","+filters could be destroyed on a worker thread when an RDS update replaced the route configuration."],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/bug_fixes/composite__destroy-route-level-filter-configs-on-main-thread.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+Fixed a race where the route level configuration of the","+:ref:`composite <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.filters.http.composite.v3.CompositePerRoute>` filter","+could be destroyed on a worker thread when an RDS update replaced the route configuration. The","+match tree, and the delegated filter configurations its actions own, are now released on the main","+thread."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"changelogs/current/bug_fixes/local_ratelimit__destroy-share-provider-manager-on-main-thread.rst","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@","+Fixed a race where the share provider manager owned by a","+:ref:`local rate limit <envoy_v3_api_msg_extensions.filters.http.local_ratelimit.v3.LocalRateLimit>`","+route level configuration could be destroyed on a worker thread. The manager is an unpinned","+singleton that owns a cluster membership callback handle, so a route level configuration may own","+the last reference to it and release it when an RDS update replaces the route configuration. It is","+now handed to the main dispatcher alongside the rate limiter, which was already posted there."],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/common/local_ratelimit/local_ratelimit_impl.cc","lines":["@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@ ShareProviderManager::ShareProviderManager(Event::Dispatcher& main_dispatcher,"," "," ShareProviderManager::~ShareProviderManager() {","   // Ensure the callback is unregistered on the main dispatcher thread.","+  if (main_dispatcher_.isThreadSafe()) {","+    handle_.reset();","+    return;","+  }","   main_dispatcher_.post([h = std::move(handle_)]() {});"," }"," "],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/aws_lambda/BUILD","lines":["@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ envoy_cc_library(","     hdrs = [\"aws_lambda_filter.h\"],","     deps = [","         \":request_response_cc_proto\",","+        \"//envoy/event:dispatcher_interface\",","         \"//envoy/http:filter_interface\",","         \"//source/common/common:base64_lib\",","         \"//source/common/common:cancel_wrapper_lib\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/aws_lambda/aws_lambda_filter.cc","lines":["@@ -28,6 +28,15 @@ namespace Extensions {"," namespace HttpFilters {"," namespace AwsLambdaFilter {"," ","+FilterSettingsImpl::~FilterSettingsImpl() {","+  if (signer_ == nullptr || main_dispatcher_.isThreadSafe()) {","+    return;","+  }","+  // A route level configuration builds its own signer, and therefore its own credentials provider","+  // chain, so releasing it may drop the last reference to a metadata based credentials provider.","+  main_dispatcher_.post([signer = std::move(signer_)]() mutable { signer.reset(); });","+}","+"," class LambdaFilterNameValues {"," public:","   Http::LowerCaseString InvocationTypeHeader{std::string{\"x-amz-invocation-type\"}};"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"source/extensions/filters/http/aws_lambda/aws_lambda_filter.h","lines":["@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@"," #include <optional>"," #include <string>"," ","+#include \"envoy/event/dispatcher.h\""," #include \"envoy/http/filt